   122	- Write the one decisive assertion that fails without the code under test, and predict the run before running it. A
   123	  first failure for any other reason means the test was written blind: stop and read again. A test is never mended to
   124	  fit the code; it changes only when the spec changes, and the spec change is recorded first.
   125	- Mutate on a scratch copy: the test must fail on the mutant while the unmutated control passes. An error is not a
   126	  catch until its traceback is read. A negative assertion ("never called") needs a mutant that makes the call on the
