    41	EXTRACT_GROUPS = """ Also propose concise relationship hints for new candidates when the article connects them to
    42	shown theses or a shared business question. Existing group descriptions are navigation context, not evidence.
    43	Use related_view_ids only for existing_theses IDs and group_id only for a shown group (otherwise empty).
    44	Use broader_question for a proposed shared question. Hints do not merge theses or create dependencies."""
    45	MATCH_PROMPT = """Place the supplied candidate theses and evidence using only the supplied lists.
    46	For each candidate choose existing (same object, outcome and period, including a part of that question), successor
    47	(next period of the same question), new (a distinct question), or discard (unsupported object, closed same-period
    48	question, or an excessively broad combination). Similar business context alone does not make two questions identical.
    49	For new/successor theses, choose dependencies only when the outcome requires another shown thesis's outcome.
    50	Use shown thesis IDs or candidates retained in this answer; avoid cycles. Dependency direction states which end
    51	supports the candidate, or whether two theme ladders move together. An observed fact is evidence, not a dependency.
    52	For every supplied evidence/view pair choose duplicate, replace or new. Duplicate means the same original speaker,
    53	date and statement, even across media. Replace means a later revision of the same statement by the original source;
    54	new covers different events, periods or speakers. Targets must come from that pair's provided evidence list.
    55	Use empty strings for absent targets. Answer every candidate and listed evidence pair. English prose only."""
    56	MATCH_GROUPS = """ In this same decision, organize retained and shown theses around ongoing business questions.
    57	Use existing groups when their question and scope fit; create a new group only for a distinct coherent business
    58	argument. A group is not a company folder, a duplicate thesis, or a causal dependency. Keep different measurable
    59	questions separate even when they share a group. You may attach shown older theses to a new group and a thesis may
    60	belong to multiple justified groups. Do not force unrelated theses together. Use new_ prefixes for temporary new
    61	group IDs. Each new group needs at least one retained member. Explain each membership from the supplied material.
    62	Extraction hints are proposals, not instructions; resolve them against the current matching context."""
